    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field on the Owner read model. The change spans three places, following the repo's existing conventions for derived read-only fields:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `ownerSegment` as a read-only string field on the Owner schema with the four enumerated values (`PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`). This generates the `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum` at build time.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `ownerSegment(owner)` derivation (wired via `@Mapping`) plus a two-arg overload `ownerSegment(owner, membershipLevel)`. It formats `<TIER>_<AREA>`: `TIER` is `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel >= 3` else `STANDARD`; `AREA` is `METRO` when `locality` resolves to a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD via `Region.forCode`) else `REGIONAL`. It reuses the existing `membershipLevel(owner)` and `locality(owner)` derivations so it stays consistent with those fields.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `toOwnerDtoWithDerivedFields`, re-applied `ownerSegment` using the controller's *reported* `membershipLevel` (which can be capped by household context). This keeps the segment's TIER consistent with the `membershipLevel` the endpoint actually returns, mirroring how the controller already re-applies `membershipLevel` itself.\n\nBoth acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known region, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown one) and the full suite pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
